{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdvbcR78xmQdPhzGn8xZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the three files for this exploratory slot, and the self-check printed `OK`. The real risk is speed: admission's full fit may not finish inside the 30-minute limit.\n\n**Model: `categorical_design_detection`**\n\n**Hypothesis.** Noticing that a sequence was deliberately constructed is an all-or-nothing verdict, not a graded impression. On each trial a person either catches a sequence as \"designed\" or doesn't. The more structural cues it has, the likelier the catch (a streak at the end, a palindrome, H/T-swapped symmetry, runs all the same length, a lopsided stretch). A sequence caught as designed is rejected by a fixed extra amount, on top of the incumbent's graded comparison of how random the two sequences look. Each person has their own threshold for making that call, drawn from a population. People with a low threshold firmly reject anything structured, and people with a high threshold rarely do. This is aimed at the critique's discrepancy that survives the FDR correction: people differ more in how often they agree with the majority than the incumbent produces (q = 0.048). The model predicts those differences show up mostly on pairs where only one sequence is structured.\n\n**Implementation.** Each sequence's graded score is the incumbent's, minus its personal pattern-detection gain. Instead of that gain, the model adds:\n- a personal detection threshold, set up the same way as the other personal parameters (non-centred, from a population);\n- one shared scale for how strongly structure drives detection;\n- one shared rejection amount (`HalfNormal`).\n\n`p_left` averages the comparison over the four combinations of \"caught as designed or not\" for the two sequences. It then mixes in the personal guessing rate and is clipped.\n\n**Self-check result**\n- The smoke fit (100 tune, 100 draws, 1 chain) gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −3459.2. That is not comparable to the incumbent's −3451.1, which comes from a full fit.\n- **Speed:** the smoke fit took 174 s for 200 iterations. The production fit runs 7,000 iterations per chain (3,000 tune + 4,000 draws) at `target_accept` 0.99. A naive extrapolation lands near the 30-minute limit, though early tuning iterations are usually the slowest. I didn't check how long the incumbent's fit takes, so I can't say whether this model is slower than models that already passed.\n- **LOO reliability:** 8.4% of trials had a high Pareto k, against a 1% tolerance. That is from a single 100-draw chain and may not hold in the full fit.\n- **Not checked:** convergence (R-hat can't be computed from one chain) and novelty against the other models.\n\nFiles are in `.../experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt`, `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":95304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":548,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32ce0bda-503e-4f12-9430-c09debe5d0a9","uuid":"e4c85b63-ae7e-4837-b82e-d6cd9dbfd15d","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:59:50.416Z","request_id":"req_011Cfdvbc2nXfWgUzr22yRVC"}
